{
  "id": "Compound::DB00169 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Cholecalciferol, also known as vitamin D3, is implicated in the regulation of steroid hormone metabolism through its interaction with steroid hydroxylase enzymes. The visible evidence suggests that Cholecalciferol binds to Cyp2r1, Cyp27a1, and Cyp11a1, all of which are involved in the steroid hydroxylase activity, which ultimately leads to the participation of Cyp2d6 in this metabolic pathway. This indicates a potential mechanism by which Cholecalciferol influences the activity of Cyp2d6, likely through the modulation of steroid hydroxylase function. The consistent presence of steroid hydroxylase activity as a central node in the interactions supports a unified mechanism involving the regulation of steroid metabolism. The evidence is robust and aligns with established biochemical pathways, suggesting that Cholecalciferol may modulate Cyp2d6 through a shared regulatory role in steroid hydroxylase activity.",
